# Completion review: Auto bands and SystemOne implementation checkpoint

Date: 2026-10-03
Scope: reviewed local implementation of `add-auto-band-seam`,
`add-auto-quality-band-filter`, `add-auto-band-demand-reserve`, and
`add-systemone-decisions-route`. Calibration implementation and local review
are complete. Real-catalog validation, production deployment/activation,
live-service checks, and OpenSpec archiving remain open.

## Decisions and implemented behavior

- Band channels default to `thrifty` only while `OMNIROUTE_AUTO_BANDS` is on.
  With the flag off, an omitted tier stays unset for upstream handling and an
  explicit tier keeps upstream behavior.
- Unrated models pass only `low`; they receive no synthetic score and stay out
  of `mid` and `high`. The old `agt` role maps to `general + tools`.
- Enabled band `thrifty` channels order eligible rungs `free → keyless →
subscription → cheap → premium`. Plain upstream `auto:thrifty` behavior is
  unchanged. Explicit `:free` retains upstream provider/model classification,
  including eligible keyless OpenCode models; it is not a per-connection
  zero-spend guarantee.
- Calibration cut points use sorted distinct numeric scores from observed
  rated models. The user approved nearest-rank selection:
  `c1 = scores[ceil(0.33*N)-1]`, `c2 = scores[ceil(0.67*N)-1]`; for nine
  distinct values, select the third and seventh. The rule is recorded in the
  quality design/spec. The calibration minimum-population guard counts
  candidates retained by each band, including unrated candidates admitted to
  `low`.
- The user approved maximum known positive monthly capacity per
  `(account, provider, poolKey)`. The disabled reserve state is a full stop:
  no source reads, calculations, refresh, diagnostics, or account narrowing.
- The user explicitly authorized deployment, production migration, and
  activation. These actions are not yet complete; they remain behind supported
  build/start and live readiness checks.

## Implementation and review

Band grammar, quality/capability filters, the selector and fallback ordering,
exact provider/model/account mappings, quota reservation, account allowlist
narrowing, reserve configuration, demand/capacity calculations, and reserve
refresh diagnostics are implemented. Disabled paths preserve upstream routing.
The account selector retains account B when a stale direct pin names A but the
authoritative allowlist is `[B]`; quota-blocked accounts remain after routable
rungs and preserve the existing final 429 when all candidates are blocked.

The confirmed quality-selection issue is fixed: strategies now run within each
billing rung, rather than allowing a global premium score or LKGP pin to outrank
eligible free candidates. The quota-cutoff regression also passes. Independent
review closed both routing findings, the quality hook, reserve configuration,
capacity behavior, and reserve integration. The identical-positive daily-cap
regression now retains one known daily axis in either catalog order; differing
positive caps still fail refresh and preserve the prior snapshot.

Three independently confirmed SystemOne defects are fixed and closed:

- Bounded BYOB reads copy small chunks without retaining near-1 MiB backing
  buffers.
- A late upstream success cannot clear a newer concurrent failure cooldown.
- Upstream error text is not persisted into call-log summaries; client error
  responses keep their specified shape.

The earlier config recovery finding is also fixed and independently verified:
7/7 focused tests cover same-mtime `EACCES` recovery and malformed-range
warning deduplication. SystemOne routing/auth alias checks found no auth seam.

Five independently confirmed calibration findings are fixed and closed:

- Manual mode now bounds/clears observed model IDs without waiting for a
  calibration run.
- The `minPerBand` guard counts unrated candidates admitted to `low`.
- Guarded-attempt timing persists so a restart does not rerun calibration
  before `intervalHours`.
- The CLI report waits for cold config loading before reading configured
  `ratedSources` and structured-output policy.
- The first request after restart uses saved ranges before constructing the
  enabled predicate, avoiding a default-range first request.

The approved formula uses nearest-rank cut points from sorted distinct numeric
scores. The focused CLI smoke used an isolated DB and returned valid JSON for 10
baseline models, 0 rated models, and no cut points; it is not a real-catalog
report.

## Verification

- Auto-Combo suite before calibration: 40 files / 353 tests passed; core and OpenSSE typechecks
  passed. Scoped checks: quality E2E 4/4, reserve source tests 25/25 across
  three suites, reserve account-routing E2E 4/4, config 13/13, capabilities
  8/8, filter 8/8, billing-rung routing 7/7, and direct upstream
  resolver/stream/quota tests 27/27. Independent review closed these slices.
- Calibration tests pass 19/19; the combined Auto-Combo and service regression
  passes 41 files / 372 tests with two workers. Core/OpenSSE typechecks,
  scoped ESLint, Prettier, and `git diff --check` pass. Default, missing, and
  unreadable configuration probes return safe defaults within three seconds.
  Independent review closed all five calibration findings; final Code
  Simplifier review found no further cleanup. An initial 20-worker run timed
  out under resource contention and reported 27 failures; the low-worker rerun
  passed. Overlapping typechecks were stopped after 16 minutes, and serial
  typechecks passed.
- SystemOne: schema/dispatch/route tests 46/46; OpenAPI coverage 8/8; route
  checker reports 276 baseline entries and 0 new findings. Core/OpenSSE
  typechecks, ESLint, Prettier, Code Simplifier, and diff checks passed.
- OpenAPI, environment references, `.env.example`, and the fork deployment
  guide were updated. `npm run check:docs-all` passed, including environment
  sync, fabricated-reference checks, and 1,180 internal links. Prettier passes
  for all changed Markdown/spec docs. Markdownlint reports the same 706
  findings in three long reference/operations docs at HEAD and in the working
  tree; changed OpenSpec/TODO docs have no findings. Repository-wide
  `npm run lint:md` reports 1,738 existing findings across 164 of 182 files.
- OpenAPI coverage passed at 97.2%; route and security-tier checks passed.
  `check:openapi-breaking` was skipped because `oasdiff` is absent and the gate
  is advisory; run it before release when the tool is available.
- The isolated-copy database rehearsal passed the three-row ledger rekey;
  missing upstream migrations were replayed and a second init reported 0
  pending. FMO data/schema remained unchanged; trigger rollback checks and
  SQLite `quick_check` passed. The runbook is
  [docs/ops/AUTO_BANDS_MIGRATION_REHEARSAL.md](docs/ops/AUTO_BANDS_MIGRATION_REHEARSAL.md).
  Production files and data were untouched.
- The reviewed reserve/SystemOne checkpoint was pushed to the feature branch as
  `0860cc7da532d50048058c97ccbb91d734f4719d`; remote SHA matched and commit
  hooks passed. The calibration slice remains uncommitted.

## Remaining gates

- Connect the built-in OmniRoute Radar client to `radar.omniroute.online`,
  verify opt-in and successful catalog sync, and confirm caches populate before
  running the real-catalog report. The current production snapshot has
  `RADAR_ENABLED` absent (default off), all `RADAR_*` overrides absent (client
  fallback is `radar.omniroute.online`), and four Radar caches empty. Public
  community-catalog access is keyless. The user will add the supporter Intel
  key through the dashboard after deployment. Bands remain on the approved
  Arena/manual score sources; Radar Intel rankings are not fed into
  `getTaskFitnessWithSource`.
- After a successful Radar/catalog sync, run the calibration report against
  the real production model catalog; record rated-source coverage, structured-
  output coverage, and candidate counts for every Hermes channel. The local
  isolated-DB CLI smoke is not production evidence. Keep manual ranges for a
  week before considering automatic recalibration.
- Validate band chat routing and full-ID `call_logs.combo_name` in a safe live
  request. Check production catalog/usage ID matches and aggregate-read cost;
  confirm candidate pools are non-empty and
  `OMNIROUTE_AUTO_FREE_FALLBACK_TO_FULL_POOL` is unset.
- Before production reserve enforcement, inspect shared daily metadata shape,
  measure refresh/read cost, and compare proposed exclusions with observed
  quota exhaustion using approved read-only validation. Keep disabled reserve
  as a full stop.
- Production uses the reviewed stock Node 26 Dockerfile; `package.json`
  supports `>=24 <27`. Node 24 portability remains a separate unchecked
  OpenSpec baseline, not a production-runtime blocker. A clean supported-
  runtime build/start is still required. The latest server reading was about
  23.17 GiB free disk, about 0.83 GiB below the 24 GiB preflight; the operator's
  resource plan is pending.
  A prior approved BuildKit cleanup reclaimed only 308,932 KiB of actual free
  space; resource readiness and deployment remain open.
- SystemOne live gates remain: confirm OpenRouter request/response shape;
  test Laya-only RU/UK, Laya stop/fallback, and 413/422 recovery followed by a
  small request; collect 50-request direct/proxy latency; verify allowed-model
  policy and production flag-off; monitor deployment variables, rollback, and
  error rows. Laya deployment and the Hermes caller switch are outside this
  repository.
- The user explicitly authorized deployment, production migration, and
  activation. The production source checkout `/opt/apps/omniroute/source` and
  Git metadata were verified clean. Deployment is pending a clean supported-
  runtime build/start. Then run the rehearsed one-time migration-ledger repair
  against a fresh consistent backup and verify integrity, idempotence, and
  rollback. Permanent migration compatibility code is forbidden.
- Correct the upstream `QuotaSnapshotRow` declaration/getter contract in a
  separate slice. The runtime getter returns camelCase fields and numeric
  `isExhausted` (`0 | 1`); the reserve code currently uses a strict local
  camelCase boundary without a compatibility shim.
- After the remaining implementation and operational gates pass, archive the
  four OpenSpec packages. Do not archive or deploy based only on local tests.
